// Russian text for the admin's schema-driven forms (lib/admin/sections.ts and
// lib/admin/pages/*): section labels and descriptions, and every field's
// label, hint, itemTitle and toggleLabel.
//
// Keyed by the English text itself, character for character — curly quotes,
// em dashes and trailing periods included. A string with no key here falls
// back to English, so a schema change never breaks the form; it just shows
// the new or edited text in English until this file is extended. When you add
// or reword a label or hint, add or rename its key here too.
//
// Placeholders in curly braces ({name}, {phone}, {area} …), %s, URLs and
// paths, RCW citations and ONARER*748K8 are kept exactly as in English. Site
// copy is English, so phrases the editor must recognise on the page (block
// headings, “bonded and insured”) stay in English with the Russian meaning
// alongside.

